course: dictionary
lesson: 13415
title: Hindquarters and the back end of an animal
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a part of a body, and the words around them tell you where that part is. «The farmer gently patted the cow's hindquarters.» The farmer is patting the cow, and the word hindquarters is near the cow's back. So hindquarters must mean the back part of the cow.
explain: «The horse's powerful hindquarters pushed it up the steep hill.» A horse pushes up a hill with its legs, not its head. So the clues say that hindquarters are the back legs and the rump, the strong back end that does the pushing.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The vet checked the dog's back legs and rump.» It still makes sense, so you know hindquarters means the back part of an animal, including the back legs and rump.
fact: Hindquarters means the back part of a four-legged animal.
fact: The hindquarters include the back legs and the rump.
fact: Horses and cows use their hindquarters to push and kick.
fact: Vets check an animal's hindquarters to see if they are healthy.
fact: Hindquarters is a plural noun, so we always write it with an s at the end.
exercise: «The horse kicked with its powerful hindquarters.» What are hindquarters? | The front feet and the head | *The back part of a four-legged animal, with the back legs and rump | The tail only | The inside of a stable
exercise: «The vet gently checked the cow's hindquarters.» Where is the vet looking? | At the cow's head and ears | *At the back legs and rump of the cow | At the milk bucket | At the gate of the field
exercise: «The horse's powerful hindquarters pushed it up the steep hill.» Find and copy one word that tells you the hindquarters are strong. | horse | *powerful | hill | pushed
test: Which part of a dog are its hindquarters? | The front paws and chest | The ears and the tail tip | The nose and mouth | *The back end, with the back legs and rump
test: Why does a vet check a horse's hindquarters? | To make it sing | To count its teeth | To choose its name | *To see if its back legs and rump are healthy
exam: A horse uses its hindquarters to | sing a song | read a book | fly into the sky | *push and kick
